@1-9
The pure model: no GUI types here. Block holds a source range and the matching comment range, both as half-open line indices.

@11-15
pair_path appends .cmt to the full source filename inside .comments.d, so foo.rs and foo.py never map to the same comment file.

@17-29
parse_marker accepts @N or @N-M on its own line. Numbers are 1-based; the function returns 0-based start and an exclusive end, and rejects zero or reversed ranges.

@31-56
parse_blocks scans the comment text for markers. Each block runs from its marker line to the line before the next marker; the final block runs to the end of the file.

@58-82
map_line translates a line from one side to the other by finding the containing block and keeping the relative position inside it. Lines outside every block are returned unchanged.

@84-94
map_scroll maps the centre of the viewport instead of the top line, so scrolling feels anchored in the middle of the screen like in meld.

@96-150
The marker helpers keep @ lines in the file but out of the visible comment pane. hide_markers blanks marker lines while preserving line numbers; restore_markers diffs the edited view against that blanked copy and puts the original markers back, reinserting any that fell inside the edited region.
